<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/sawtooth.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/sawtooth-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/sawtooth.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Service areas</span></nav><p class="kicker">Statewide coverage</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal Across All 44 Idaho Counties</h1><p class="lede">Idaho Insurance Appraiser works statewide, from the Canadian border to the Bear River. These 12 area pages cover the communities where we handle claims most often.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-w" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section>
<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="igrid" data-stagger><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/boise-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/hero.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hero-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hero.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Ada County</span><h2>Boise</h2><p>Boise packs a century of housing into one valley, from 1910s bungalows to new homes pressed against the foothills. Each era fails differently in a storm or a fire, and each needs its own estimate.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/meridian-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/neighborhood.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/neighborhood-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/neighborhood.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Ada County</span><h2>Meridian</h2><p>Meridian grew from a farm town into one of Idaho’s largest cities in a single generation. Its newer subdivisions share builders, materials and roof designs, so one storm can mean hundreds of similar claims.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/nampa-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/farm-barn.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/farm-barn-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/farm-barn.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="960" height="639" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Canyon County</span><h2>Nampa</h2><p>Nampa mixes a historic downtown, fast-growing subdivisions and working farmland. A single storm can hit a 1920s house, a new two-story and a pole barn in the same afternoon.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/caldwell-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/farmland.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/farmland-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/farmland.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="702" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Canyon County</span><h2>Caldwell</h2><p>Caldwell is the Canyon County seat, home to the College of Idaho and gateway to the Sunnyslope wine country. Its claims range from older homes near Indian Creek to farm buildings on the bench.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/eagle-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/home-exterior-2.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/home-exterior-2-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/home-exterior-2.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Ada County</span><h2>Eagle</h2><p>Eagle’s custom homes use high-end roofing, finishes and systems that standard estimate pricing often misses. When those homes are damaged, the details decide the claim.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/idaho-falls-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/idaho-falls.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/idaho-falls-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/idaho-falls.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Bonneville County</span><h2>Idaho Falls</h2><p>Idaho Falls sits on the Upper Snake River Plain, where summer hail, strong wind and deep winter cold all take turns. Claims here often involve more than one peril on the same building.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/pocatello-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/pocatello.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/pocatello-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/pocatello.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Bannock County</span><h2>Pocatello</h2><p>Pocatello sits where the Portneuf River leaves the mountains, and the wind knows it. Canyon gusts, summer storms and hillside fire risk all shape claims here.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/rexburg-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snow-house.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snow-house-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snow-house.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Madison County</span><h2>Rexburg</h2><p>Rexburg is a college town on the Upper Snake plain, with a large stock of student apartments, family homes and surrounding farms. Cold winters and strong wind drive most claims here.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/twin-falls-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/twin-falls.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/twin-falls-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/twin-falls.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Twin Falls County</span><h2>Twin Falls</h2><p>Twin Falls sits on the rim of the Snake River Canyon, the commercial center of the Magic Valley. Wind and summer storms cross its farmland freely, and claims often reach well beyond town.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/coeur-d-alene-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/coeur-d-alene.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/coeur-d-alene-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/coeur-d-alene.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Kootenai County</span><h2>Coeur d’Alene</h2><p>Coeur d’Alene’s lake, forests and fast growth create a distinct claim profile: falling trees in windstorms, heavy snow and ice, and smoke from summer fires.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/lewiston-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/lewiston.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/lewiston-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/lewiston.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Nez Perce County</span><h2>Lewiston</h2><p>Lewiston sits at the confluence of the Snake and Clearwater rivers, Idaho’s lowest-elevation city. Its mild winters and hot summers give it a different claim profile from the rest of the state.</p></span></a><a class="icard rv" href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/ketchum-insurance-appraiser/"><span class="icard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/sun-valley.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/sun-valley-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/sun-valley.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><span class="icard-k"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13S3 17 3 10a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>Blaine County</span><h2>Ketchum &amp; Sun Valley</h2><p>Ketchum and Sun Valley combine heavy mountain snow, wildfire exposure and high-value second homes. Claims here need estimates that reflect mountain construction costs.</p></span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head left rv"><p class="kicker dark">Regions</p><h2>How claims differ across Idaho</h2><p>The same policy language plays out very differently in a Ketchum chalet, a Meridian two-story and a Coeur d’Alene lake cabin.</p></div><div class="rrows" data-stagger><div class="rrow rv"><h3>Treasure Valley</h3><p class="region-c">Boise · Meridian · Nampa · Caldwell · Eagle</p><p>Idaho’s population center packs historic Boise homes, fast-growing subdivisions and working farms into one valley. Summer storms, foothills fire and January cold snaps drive most claims.</p></div><div class="rrow rv"><h3>North Idaho</h3><p class="region-c">Coeur d’Alene · Post Falls · Sandpoint</p><p>Forests, lakes and deeper winters. Wind-thrown trees, snow-loaded roofs and ice dams lead the list, with lake homes and vacation rentals adding coverage wrinkles.</p></div><div class="rrow rv"><h3>Lewis-Clark &amp; Palouse</h3><p class="region-c">Lewiston · Moscow · Orofino</p><p>Idaho’s lowest, warmest valley meets the rolling Palouse. Canyon winds, grass fires and summer storms shape claims on older hillside homes and university rentals.</p></div><div class="rrow rv"><h3>Wood River &amp; Central Mountains</h3><p class="region-c">Ketchum · Sun Valley · Hailey · McCall</p><p>Mountain construction costs, second homes left empty for weeks and some of the state’s heaviest snow loads. Wildfire season follows the melt.</p></div><div class="rrow rv"><h3>Magic Valley</h3><p class="region-c">Twin Falls · Jerome · Burley</p><p>The canyon-rim city and its agricultural hinterland: dairies, storage buildings and growing subdivisions, all exposed to wind across open ground.</p></div><div class="rrow rv"><h3>Eastern Idaho</h3><p class="region-c">Idaho Falls · Pocatello · Rexburg</p><p>Long winters on the Upper Snake plain, wind through the Portneuf Gap and summer hail. Student apartments, potato cellars and older neighborhoods all see claims.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-in rv"><div><h2>Don’t see your town?</h2><p>We cover every Idaho county. Call and tell us where the property is.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-w" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
</main>
